    "background_story": "In the sleepy village of Ashwood, Chaim was known as a mysterious and feared figure. The elderly villagers whispered tales of his supposed dealings with dark magic, and how he had made a pact with a malevolent hag who dwelled in the nearby forest. They claimed that Chaim's unusual abilities to heal and divine were a result of the hag's influence. While some believed him to be a wicked sorcerer, others saw him as a guardian who kept the forces of darkness at bay. Chaim's true nature remained shrouded in mystery, but one thing was certain: his powers were real, and those who crossed him would face the wrath of the hag. As the years passed, the villagers learned to respect and fear Chaim, never daring to test the limits of his powers or the wrath of his supposed patron.",
